@startuml sell-orchestrator-vs-aggregate
!include sell-style.puml
title <size:12><color:#087F8C>05 / RESPONSIBILITIES</color></size>\nGive each decision one home

top to bottom direction
rectangle "<b>Application service</b>\nLoad portfolio · fetch quote\nDelegate sale · persist state and history" as S #EAF3F9
rectangle "<b>Portfolio</b>\nsell(ticker, quantity, price)\n\nValidate the command and holding\nCredit cash by the sale proceeds" as P #E6F3F1
rectangle "<b>Holding</b>\nsell(quantity, price)\n\nCheck available shares\nConsume lots in FIFO order" as H #E6F3F1
rectangle "<b>Lot</b>\ncalculateCostBasis(take) · reduce(take)\n\nCalculate purchase cost\nCheck and reduce remaining shares" as L #E6F3F1
S -down-> P
P -down-> H
H -down-> L
note bottom of L
  Portfolio, Holding and Lot form one aggregate.
  Application mutations should enter through Portfolio.
end note
@enduml
